A||N||3||Linx||torque converter fill?||||1||
Z||000000||Linx||01-08-2001||02:56 PM||||During the rebuild of my V6, I spilled some of the torque converter's fluid. Alot, actually.  I didnt worry about it because I assumed that the tranny fluid change would replenish the t.c.<P>Well, now (months after the rebuld) my car wont move.  Runs great, but stepping on the gas wont get me anywhere.  Tranny fluid level is normal, but now Im wondering if the converter should have been filled?<P>Dumb one; where's the converter get its fluid from?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Boxdin||01-08-2001||06:32 PM||||Absolutely fill as much of the converter as you can before you install it. It will self pump, but it may go for a bit of time before it fills up, and could be damaged.  your question could be- is there an air bubble in it, good question. ||||reg||6
Z||000002||theogre||01-08-2001||07:20 PM||||The TC is filled by the tranny pump. Total tranny volume from a dry fill is 9 quarts including what the TC drinks.<P>If the tranny is dead something was going bad that would have died anyway. As long as you had enough oil in the TC to lube it at startup it will fill fairly quickly.<P>The TC will not air lock unless there is a major transmission problem. The oil is heavy and displaces the air to the center of the TC where it is then forced out of the converter.<P>One thing you can do is check the fluid before you start it then again after. The fluid level should drop very quickly into the full range. If it doesn't then you've probly fried the pump. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||01-09-2001||12:14 AM||||Obviously it's not a Fiero, but they all work basically the same way.  The Ford dealer recommends draining the converter when changing the filter in my T-bird.  It has a drain plug just for this.  Then they just add about 5 quarts via the dipstick, start it and idle in park, and add the other 8 quarts. Mine's been done that way twice, with no problems, so I don't think the converter isn't filling back up.||||reg||1
